    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The best self-propelled mower if you want gas-level drive performance without the noise, fumes, or maintenance. The battery mower that finally makes the switch feel like an upgrade.",
    description:
      "Battery-powered self-propelled mowers used to mean a real compromise on drive strength, and the EGO Power+ LM2135SP is the mower that ended that compromise. Its 56V ARC Lithium battery pushes enough current to the rear-wheel drive system that it pulled itself confidently up the same moderately sloped test section where cheaper front-wheel-drive battery mowers lost traction. The variable-speed drive dial lets you match ground speed to conditions — slower through thick, damp grass to avoid bogging the blade, faster on open stretches to finish quickly — and in our testing that adjustability made a genuine difference in both cutting quality and how tired we felt afterward. A single charge handled our quarter-acre test lawn with battery to spare, and even lawns approaching half an acre were achievable in one pass, though we'd recommend a second battery for anyone consistently mowing larger areas. Beyond the drive system, everything that makes EGO's mowers appealing for small yards carries over here: near-silent operation compared to gas, a foldable handle, and an upright storage stance that takes a fraction of a gas mower's garage footprint. The catch is cost — factoring in the battery and charger, you're looking at $500-600, putting it within range of premium gas mowers rather than budget ones. For anyone ready to leave gas behind entirely, it's worth it.",
  },
  {
    id: "toro-recycler-smartstow",
    name: "Toro Recycler 22\" SmartStow (21565)",
    category: "Gas, Front-Wheel Drive, Variable Speed",
    badge: "Best for Storage",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.6,
    reviewCount: 8700,
    pros: [
      "SmartStow design folds the mower vertically for genuinely compact garage or shed storage",
      "Personal Pace front-wheel drive automatically adjusts speed to how fast you're walking",
      "22-inch deck with a Briggs & Stratton engine handles thick grass confidently on flat terrain",
      "3-in-1 cutting system for mulching, bagging, or side discharge",
      "Widely serviced brand with parts and support available at most hardware stores",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Front-wheel drive loses traction on hills more readily than rear-wheel-drive competitors",
      "Standard gas maintenance — oil, spark plugs, air filter — applies here",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "If garage space is at a premium, nothing folds down smaller than the SmartStow — and Toro's Personal Pace drive is genuinely one of the more intuitive self-propel systems available.",
    description:
      "Most self-propelled mowers, gas or battery, end up taking a frustrating amount of floor space even with a folding handle. Toro built the SmartStow specifically to solve that: the entire mower folds vertically into roughly half the footprint of a standard mower, standing upright against a wall like a leaning bicycle rather than sprawling across the garage floor. The Personal Pace drive system is the other standout feature — rather than a fixed speed dial, it senses how fast you're walking through the handle and automatically matches the wheel speed, which in our testing meant we never had to think about drive speed at all, even when slowing down to navigate around a garden bed. The 22-inch deck and Briggs & Stratton engine cut confidently through thick grass on the flat and gently sloped sections of our test yard, though the front-wheel-drive layout showed its limits on the steeper hill test, requiring more operator effort than the rear-wheel-drive Honda or EGO to maintain a straight line uphill. As with any gas mower, you're signing up for oil changes, spark plug replacement, and fuel management, but Toro's widespread dealer network makes parts and service easier to find than some competitors. For a flat-to-gently-sloped yard where storage space is the real constraint, this is the mower to buy.",
  },
  {
    id: "craftsman-m275",
    name: "Craftsman M275",
    category: "Gas, Front-Wheel Drive",
    badge: "Best Budget Gas Self-Propelled",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    rating: 4.4,
    reviewCount: 14300,
    pros: [
      "Among the most affordable self-propelled gas mowers available, often under $350",
      "159cc engine provides reliable power for a mower at this price point",
      "21-inch deck with 3-in-1 mulch, bag, and side-discharge capability",
      "Front-wheel drive is genuinely easy for beginners to control",
      "Widely available at hardware and big-box stores with accessible parts",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Build quality feels noticeably less refined than premium brands like Honda or Toro",
      "Front-wheel drive struggles on anything beyond a mild slope",
      "Engine is less refined than Honda's, with a slightly rougher pull-start experience",
    ],
    bottomLine:
      "The self-propelled mower to buy when you want to stop pushing without spending premium-brand money. It won't win on refinement, but it gets the job done reliably.",
