      "Not every self-propelled mower needs to be optimized for hills — on a large, genuinely flat lawn, what actually matters is covering ground efficiently without wearing yourself out, and the Troy-Bilt TB230 does that well. Its 163cc engine and 21-inch deck moved through our open, flat test area at a confident pace, and the front-wheel-drive system, while not the strongest choice for hills, worked exactly as intended on level ground, requiring minimal operator effort to keep the mower tracking straight. The dual-lever height adjustment system, one lever per axle pair rather than a single central lever, adjusts height quickly and held its setting reliably through repeated testing, a detail that matters more than it sounds like on a mower you're adjusting seasonally. Starting was consistent across our test sessions, and the overall build felt sturdy for the price point, without the flimsier plastic components we noticed on some cheaper competitors. Where it falls short is exactly where you'd expect a front-wheel-drive gas mower to: our hill test showed clear traction loss compared to the rear-wheel-drive Honda and Snapper, and gas engine noise is simply louder than any battery mower we tested, an increasingly relevant factor for anyone mowing early morning or in a close-quartered neighborhood. For a large, flat property, it's a genuinely dependable, well-priced choice.",
  },
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Self-Propelled Lawn Mowers",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-self-propelled-lawn-mower/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What is the best self-propelled lawn mower?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For most homeowners, the Honda HRX217VKA offers the best overall combination of drive strength, hill performance, and long-term reliability. For a quieter, battery-powered option with comparable drive performance, the EGO Power+ LM2135SP is the top pick. For yards with genuine hills, the Snapper SP80 82V delivers the strongest traction of any battery mower tested.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is front-wheel drive or rear-wheel drive better for a self-propelled mower?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Rear-wheel drive provides significantly better traction on hills and uneven terrain because the mower's weight naturally shifts backward while pushing, increasing grip on the drive wheels. Front-wheel drive is simpler, often cheaper, and performs fine on flat or gently sloped yards, but loses traction more readily on real inclines.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are battery self-propelled mowers as powerful as gas?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Modern high-voltage battery mowers, particularly 56V and 80V+ platforms, now deliver drive torque and cutting power comparable to mid-tier gas mowers for lawns up to roughly half an acre. Gas retains an edge in unlimited runtime and typically slightly stronger performance in extremely thick or tall grass, but the practical gap has narrowed significantly.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Do I need a self-propelled mower for a small, flat yard?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not necessarily. Self-propulsion adds the most value on larger lawns, hilly or uneven terrain, and for anyone with physical limitations that make pushing a mower difficult. On a small, flat yard under a quarter acre, a lighter push mower is often easier to maneuver around obstacles and cheaper to buy.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How does variable-speed drive work on a self-propelled mower?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Variable-speed drive lets you adjust how fast the wheels pull the mower forward independent of the engine or motor speed, typically via a dial or a walk-sensing system like Toro's Personal Pace. This lets you slow down for careful maneuvering around obstacles while keeping full cutting power, then speed up on open stretches to finish faster.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "How much does a good self-propelled lawn mower cost?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Budget gas self-propelled mowers start around $300-350, mid-range gas and value battery mowers run $400-550, and premium gas or battery models with rear-wheel drive and variable speed typically cost $600-900 including a battery and charger where applicable.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Home Fix Reviews" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
      review: {
        "@type": "Review",
        reviewBody: product.bottomLine,
        author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
        publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Home Fix Reviews" },
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home & Yard Care",
    tags: [
      "self propelled lawn mower",
      "gas lawn mower",
      "battery lawn mower",
      "rear wheel drive mower",
      "lawn care",
      "home improvement",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div
        class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10"
        style="background-image: url('data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg width=\'60\' height=\'60\' viewBox=\'0 0 60 60\' xmlns=\'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\'%3E%3Cg fill=\'none\' fill-rule=\'evenodd\'%3E%3Cg fill=\'%23ffffff\' fill-opacity=\'1\'%3E%3Cpath d=\'M36 34v-4h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2h-4zm0-30V0h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2V6h4V4h-4zM6 34v-4H4v4H0v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2H6zM6 4V0H4v4H0v2h4v4h2V6h4V4H6z\'/%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/svg%3E');"
      ></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Updated August 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          The 7 Best <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Self-Propelled Lawn Mowers</span> in 2026
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          We tested 12+ self-propelled mowers on hills, thick grass, and uneven terrain over a full mowing season — gas and battery, front-wheel and rear-wheel drive. Only 7 earned a spot. Here's what actually pulls its own weight.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#honda-hrx217vka"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#drive-types"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Drive System Guide
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Alex Rivers</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Home Improvement Editor</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="7.9k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1E90FF" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="8" y1="6" x2="21" y2="6"></line><line x1="8" y1="12" x2="21" y2="12"></line><line x1="8" y1="18" x2="21" y2="18"></line><line x1="3" y1="6" x2="3.01" y2="6"></line><line x1="3" y1="12" x2="3.01" y2="12"></line><line x1="3" y1="18" x2="3.01" y2="18"></line></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. Our 7 Top Picks Reviewed</a>
          <a href="#why-self-propelled" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. Self-Propelled Mower Buying Guide</a>
          <a href="#drive-types" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Front-Wheel vs Rear-Wheel Drive</a>
          <a href="#gas-vs-battery" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Gas vs Battery Self-Propelled Mowers</a>
          <a href="#choosing-speed" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Self-Propelled Mowers for Hills</a>
          <a href="#cost-of-ownership" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Self-Propelled Mower Cost of Ownership</a>
          <a href="#maintenance" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Self-Propelled Mower Maintenance & Repairs</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
